const goddesses = [
 ['Shailaputri',0,'Daughter of the mountains','Born as the daughter of the mountain king Himavan, Parvati is honoured as Shailaputri. Riding a bull, she carries a lotus and a trident. Her story begins a journey of devotion.','Begin with courage.'],
 ['Brahmacharini',1,'A journey of devotion','Parvati practised deep meditation to be united with Shiva. Through years of patient effort, she stayed true to her purpose. Her prayer beads and water pot remind us of this simple, devoted life.','Great things take patience.'],
 ['Chandraghanta',2,'Courage with a gentle heart','When Shiva arrived for their wedding in a fearsome form, Parvati met the moment with courage. As Chandraghanta, she wears a crescent shaped like a bell and protects those who seek her help.','Be brave. Be kind.'],
 ['Kushmanda',3,'A smile that brought light','In a traditional creation story, the universe was dark and silent. Kushmanda smiled, and light and life began to blossom. She is celebrated as the creative energy that nourishes the world.','Let your creativity shine.'],
 ['Skandamata',4,'The strength of a mother’s love','Skandamata is Parvati as the mother of Skanda, also known as Kartikeya or Murugan. She holds her child while riding a lion: a picture of tender care and powerful protection together.','Caring for others is a strength.'],
 ['Katyayani',5,'Standing up for what is right','Sage Katyayana prayed for the Goddess to be born as his daughter. As Katyayani, she became a mighty protector. With the strength of Durga, she challenged Mahishasura and defended the world.','Use your strength to help others.'],
 ['Kalaratri',6,'A protector through the darkness','When harmful forces threatened the world, the Goddess took the powerful form of Kalaratri. Her fierce appearance frightens evil, while her raised hand reassures her devotees: do not be afraid.','Courage can help us face our fears.'],
 ['Mahagauri',7,'Peace after perseverance','After Parvati’s long years of meditation, a refreshing bath washed away the dust of her journey. She is honoured as radiant Mahagauri, a peaceful form associated with renewal and blessings.','Make room for a fresh beginning.'],
 ['Siddhidatri',8,'The giver of blessings','Seated on a lotus, Siddhidatri is revered as the giver of spiritual accomplishments, called siddhis. Tradition tells that even Shiva received her blessings. She completes our journey through the nine forms of Durga.','Keep learning. Share what you learn.']
];
